@page "/utforsker"
@using Fhi.Munin.Explorer.Blazor

<PageTitle>Modern host — utforskeren</PageTitle>

<div class="hostchrome">
    <p class="hostchrome-note">
        <code>VariableExplorer</code> — the whole variabelutforsker, and the one component a host
        normally mounts: search, the reader's own variable lists behind the second tab, and the view
        in the address bar. <a href="/">The front page</a> mounts <code>VariableSearch</code>, the
        search half on its own, because it receives Kelda's handover as a <code>Filter</code>
        parameter and so has to own its own query string.
    </p>
    <p class="hostchrome-note">
        <code>IsAuthenticated</code> is hardcoded <code>true</code> here. This sample has no sign-in,
        and the Variabelliste tab renders nothing at all for a signed-out reader — the package has no
        business wording a sign-in prompt for a host. Saying so at the mount point is how the tab has
        anything in it to look at.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="hostframe">
    @* prerender: false, like every other mount in this sample — and here it is not a preference:
       the component owns the query string and throws on initialisation if it is prerendered,
       rather than drawing a page whose URL never follows the view. *@
    <VariableExplorer Language="no"
                      IsAuthenticated="true"
                      @rendermode="@(new InteractiveServerRenderMode(prerender: false))" />
</div>
